        {
          "text": "closure of a 3-braid L. Then one of the following holds:",
          "bbox": [
            72.0,
            477.88,
            337.06,
            488.79
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMMI10",
            "CMTI10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            10.91
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "(1) L has braid index 3 and every 3-braid which represents L is conjugate to L.",
          "bbox": [
            79.92,
            511.6,
            460.66,
            522.81
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMMI10",
            "CMR10",
            "CMSY10",
            "CMTI10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            10.91
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "(2) L has braid index 3, and is represented by exactly two distinct conjugacy classes of closed",
          "bbox": [
            79.92,
            533.2,
            539.93,
            544.41
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMR10",
            "CMSY10",
            "CMTI10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            10.91
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "3-braids. This happens if and only if the conjugacy class of L contains a braid which admits",
          "bbox": [
            99.24,
            546.76,
            539.77,
            557.67
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMMI10",
            "CMTI10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            10.91
          ]
        },
        {
